From 38f6d485689684cc1aba1abeecffaea2b5254d36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harshanandak <harshanandak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:10:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] docs: reconcile three self-contradictions in the shipping
 rules
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- AGENTS.md listed three must-fix classes (secrets, injection, broken build)
  while review.md added a fourth for inaccurate documentation. The fourth is
  the intended rule — a doc promising an enforcement or command that does not
  exist makes future agents stop checking, which is most of what this PR is
  fixing — so AGENTS.md now states it and review.md matches. Everything else
  valid is still filed, not built.
- ship.md marked the beads issue done in Step 3, before the push and before
  gh pr create. A failure in either left an issue completed with no PR, and
  /ship's own entry gate then refuses the retry because it wants in_progress.
  Moved to after PR creation, with an explicit restore-on-failure line.
- premerge.md's exit gate said "Do NOT suggest merging" while Step 5 requires
  asking the user to squash-and-merge, so every successful run had to break
  one or the other. The gate now forbids executing a merge and explicitly
  requires the handoff.

Found by codex review on PR #132.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
